Round 27 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Generalized direct compiled-call lowering from self-only to any known compiled ref.
- Added `aot_emit_compiled_fun_name(...)` helper to resolve `ref_id -> F_<name>` only when the callee is actually compiled (`id` bounds, `BOOK[id] != 0`, `table_get != NULL`).
- Added `aot_emit_prototypes(...)` and now emit forward declarations for all generated `F_*` functions before definitions.
- `aot_emit_try_demanded_ref_call(...)` now uses guarded direct calls for all compiled refs (not just `self`), preserving:
  - `STEPS_ITRS_LIM == 0` gate,
  - depth fallback (`aot_call_depth() >= AOT_MAX_DEPTH` -> `term_new_ref(ref_id)`),
  - `AOT_CALL_DEPTH++/--` and `aot_heap_compiled_enter()/leave()`,
  - leftover arg reapply loop (`for (j = call_pos; j > 0; j--) term_new_app(...)`).
- Head-position `REF` (`aot_emit_node(..., head=1)`) now also direct-calls compiled refs under the same guards; tail-self-loop `continue` optimization is preserved.

Why this mattered
- Runtime dispatch (`aot_call_ref` table lookup) remained on hot cross-def call paths even after self-call optimization.
- This completes the obvious dispatch elimination pass: compiled code now calls compiled code directly whenever possible.

Validation
- Build: `cd clang && clang -O2 -o main main.c`.
- Tests: `./test/_all_.sh` passed.
- Canary deopt parity: `HVM_AOT_DEOPT=1 --as-c -s -T1` kept `AOT_DEOPT total=0` on sampled benches.
- Generated C check (`gab_takl --to-c`):
  - now emits prototype block (`static Term F_...(...)`) at top,
  - emits direct cross-def calls (e.g. `F_mas`, `F_mas_go`, `F_len`),
  - sampled generated programs show `aot_call_ref(` count = `0`.

